id:                     E6408
trigger_tool:           conan|python|meson
phase:                  dependency-install|generate|cross-build
error_signature:        OHOS Meson builds require an absolute C compiler path|absolute archiver path

severity:               2
category:               conan|cross-build|path-semantics|meson
match_keywords:         Conan install, Windows host, OHOS target, os.path.isabs, posixpath.isabs, compiler_executables, Meson archiver, target-only tool, build never
title:                  Validate OHOS target tool paths with POSIX semantics and defer target filesystem checks

root_cause:             Python os.path follows the host platform. During a Windows-hosted OHOS Conan install, os.path.isabs rejects a valid /data/... target path and os.path.isfile queries the wrong filesystem. Generator time needs a syntactically valid target tool path for the Meson cross file, while target existence and executability are build-time properties.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 recipes that generate cross-build files on Windows for OHOS or another POSIX target and read compiler or auxiliary tool paths from tools.build:compiler_executables.
verification_cmd:       In a fresh isolated OHOS/armv8 Conan home, run graph info and install --build=never with absolute POSIX compiler paths; require install RC0, then run the production install with relative compiler and relative explicit archiver profiles and require distinct fail-closed RCs and messages.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           target-posix-path-generation-build-time-existence
rec_description:        Resolve target compiler and archiver values with posixpath.isabs/dirname/join during generate(), emit the exact POSIX archiver into the Meson toolchain, and reuse the same resolver in build() before checking os.path.isfile and os.access on the target host.
rec_command:            use posixpath for target path syntax in generate(); require file and X_OK at the start of build()
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      explicit-target-archiver-profile
fallback_description:   If the archiver is not adjacent to the target compiler, require an explicit absolute POSIX ar entry in tools.build:compiler_executables and keep the same build-time existence gate.
fallback_command:       tools.build:compiler_executables={"c":"/target/bin/clang","cpp":"/target/bin/clang++","ar":"/target/bin/llvm-ar"}
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          profile-and-recipe

forbid_1_pattern:       os\.path\.isabs\(.*/data|ntpath\.isabs\(.*/data
forbid_1_reason:        Host path semantics cannot validate the syntax of a POSIX target path.
forbid_1_consequence:   A complete dependency graph downloads successfully but root generator finalization fails on Windows.
forbid_2_pattern:       generate\(\).*os\.path\.(isfile|exists|isdir).*compiler|generate\(\).*os\.access.*X_OK
forbid_2_reason:        Generator execution can occur off target and must not require target-only tool files on the host filesystem.
forbid_2_consequence:   W0 dependency materialization is conflated with target build readiness, while the actual build can still lack a reliable gate.

principles:             P005,P010
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E296,E307]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

